        "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/infant-toddler-nutrition/breastfeeding/how-much-and-how-often.html",
        "description": "Your baby will breastfeed about 8 to 12 times in 24 hours. Babies fed breast milk exclusively or receiving <strong>less than 32 ounces of infant formula per day</strong> need extra vitamin D, starting shortly after birth.",
