        "title": "Readiness for Babies to Start Solid Food - Solid Starts",
        "url": "https://solidstarts.com/readiness/",
        "description": "Most full-term babies are ready around 6 months of age, though some are ready a bit earlier and some a few weeks later. For premature babies, look for signs of readiness around 6 months chronological age. Check out When to Start Solids with Preemies for more guidance. You may be told to introduce rice cereal and purees around 4 months of age, but this is outdated advice.",
        "position": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "4 signs your baby is ready for solids",
        "url": "https://www.kidecology.com/baby-ready-for-solids.html",
        "description": "From a gross motor and oral motor development perspective, main signs of readiness are <strong>the ability to sit upright and the disappearance of the tongue-thrust reflex</strong>.2 It’s also important to consider babies’ interest in table foods and their ...",
        "position": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Introducing Solids: Signs of Readiness",
        "url": "https://www.happyfamilyorganics.com/learning-center/article/introducing-solids-signs-of-readiness/",
        "description": "Wait to start solids until your baby is ready. Signs include <strong>head control, ability to sit up, and interest in food</strong>.",
        "position": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Signs of readiness for solids — Ready Set Grow",
        "url": "https://www.readysetgrownutrition.com/blog/signs-of-readiness-for-solids",
